---
const {base}=Astro.props;
const moments=['The invitation','Across the table','The experience','The language','Boundaries','Creative Brief'];
const briefLabels={intention:'The central intention',people:'The people it may serve',experience:'The experience',voice:'The editorial voice',principles:'My creative principles',scope:'The scope',questions:'Questions to carry forward'};
---
<section data-chapter-panel="foundation" hidden class="chapter-foundation">
 <nav class="chapter-moments" aria-label="Foundation moments">{moments.map((name,i)=><button type="button" data-document-moment="foundation" data-step={i}>{name}</button>)}</nav>
 <section data-document-panel="foundation" data-step="0"><p class="studio-eyebrow">Section two · The Foundation</p><h2>What do you want your cards to make possible?</h2><p class="chapter-intro">A deck can invite reflection, help someone make sense of an experience, teach a method, offer guidance, celebrate beauty, tell a story, or introduce a completely new way of seeing something familiar.</p><p>There is no need to decide on a single purpose. Think about what you hope becomes possible when someone spends time with your work.</p><label class="studio-field">What I want to offer<textarea data-foundation-response="intention" rows="5"/></label><details><summary>If several purposes are emerging</summary><label class="studio-field">Which would you most regret losing if you simplified the project?<textarea data-foundation-response="essential" rows="4"/></label></details></section>
 <section data-document-panel="foundation" data-step="1" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">The person across the table</p><h2>Who will encounter your work?</h2><p class="chapter-intro">Imagine someone sitting down with your finished deck. Who are they, what might have brought them to it, and what would you like them to find there?</p><label class="studio-field">The person, or people, I am imagining<textarea data-foundation-response="people" rows="8"/></label><details><summary>Consider the setting, if it helps</summary><p>Your deck may be just for you, used independently, shared with experienced readers or introduced by a facilitator. There is no need for a commercial audience.</p><label class="studio-field">Where and how might they use it? What context or support may they need?<textarea data-foundation-response="context" rows="5"/></label></details></section>
 <section data-document-panel="foundation" data-step="2" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">The first encounter</p><h2>What does using this deck feel like?</h2><p>Imagine your deck is finished. Someone is using it for the first time. What would you like that moment to be like?</p><label class="studio-field">A first encounter<textarea data-foundation-response="encounter" rows="8"/></label><details><summary>Find a few words for the experience</summary><p>Quiet and reflective, playful and curious, structured and methodical, immersive and symbolic, creative and surprising — or something else entirely.</p><label class="studio-field">What can the deck responsibly promise, and what is outside that promise?<textarea data-foundation-response="promise" rows="5"/></label><p>A useful invitation need not promise a guaranteed outcome.</p></details></section>
 <section data-document-panel="foundation" data-step="3" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">The language of your work</p><h2>How will your deck communicate?</h2><p>If someone read the words without seeing the imagery, what qualities would you hope they recognized?</p><label class="studio-field">My editorial voice<textarea data-foundation-response="voice" rows="7"/></label><details><summary>Explore your voice compass</summary><p>These are invitations to think, not scores or rules:</p><ul><li>Direct and clear ↔ poetic and evocative</li><li>Open and exploratory ↔ structured and defined</li><li>Gentle and invitational ↔ bold and challenging</li><li>Everyday and accessible ↔ layered and specialized</li></ul><label class="studio-field">Terminology, conventions or an existing method I want to use<textarea data-foundation-response="conventions" rows="4"/></label></details><label class="studio-field">The creative principles I want to preserve<textarea data-foundation-response="principles" rows="4" placeholder="Perhaps clarity, symbolic depth, cultural accuracy, or respect for the reader's autonomy…"/></label></section>
 <section data-document-panel="foundation" data-step="4" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">The creative boundaries</p><h2>What belongs here — and what can wait?</h2><p>Keep possibilities without asking this one deck to hold them all. You can move ideas between these spaces as your thinking changes.</p>{[['heart','At the heart','Essential ideas, themes and qualities.'],['exploring','Still exploring','Possibilities that need more thought, research or experimentation.'],['deferred','For another time','Ideas to keep for a future project or edition.']].map(([key,label,help])=><label class="studio-field">{label}<small>{help}</small><textarea data-foundation-response={key} rows="4"/></label>)}<details><summary>Responsibility and open questions</summary><p>Consider permissions, attribution, cultural knowledge or specialist contributions when relevant. This space records questions; it does not provide clearance.</p><label class="studio-field">Responsibilities to explore<textarea data-foundation-response="responsibility" rows="4"/></label><label class="studio-field">Questions to carry forward<textarea data-foundation-response="questions" rows="4"/></label></details></section>
 <section data-document-panel="foundation" data-step="5" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">An evolving editorial foundation</p><h2>My Creative Brief</h2><p>Bring your own words together, then edit this brief until it expresses your current direction. Original reflections and earlier saved versions remain available.</p><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-assemble="foundation">Bring my words into the brief</button>{Object.entries(briefLabels).map(([key,label])=><label class="studio-field">{label}<textarea data-foundation-output={key} rows="4" placeholder=""/></label>)}<details><summary>Original Foundation reflections</summary><div data-original-document="foundation"/></details><details><summary>Earlier saved briefs</summary><div data-document-history="foundation"/></details><h3>Your vision is becoming a creative direction.</h3><p>Your Creative Brief is here to guide your decisions, not confine them.</p><button class="studio-button" type="button" data-chapter="architecture">Explore The Architecture</button></section>
 <div class="chapter-actions"><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-save-document>Save my Foundation</button><button type="button" class="studio-button" data-document-next="foundation">Continue</button></div><a class="chapter-workshop" href={`${base}/`}>Open My Workshop at any time</a>
</section>
<style>.chapter-moments{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.35rem;margin-bottom:1.8rem}.chapter-moments button{background:none;border:0;border-bottom:2px solid transparent;padding:.5rem .35rem;font:inherit;color:inherit}.chapter-moments button[aria-current]{border-color:#526b59;font-weight:700}.chapter-foundation h2{font:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.5rem)/1.2 'Playfair Display',Georgia,serif}.chapter-foundation p{line-height:1.75}.chapter-intro{font-size:1.14rem}.chapter-foundation textarea{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;font:400 1rem/1.65 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;padding:.8rem;color:#242b2b;background:#fff;border:1px solid #9d9e94;border-radius:4px;resize:vertical}.chapter-foundation .studio-field{display:grid;gap:.55rem;margin:1.3rem 0;font-weight:600}.chapter-foundation small{font-weight:400}.chapter-foundation details{border-top:1px solid #cec9c1;padding:1rem 0}.chapter-foundation summary{cursor:pointer;line-height:1.5;font-weight:600}.chapter-actions{display:flex;gap:.7rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:2rem 0 1rem}.chapter-workshop{display:block;margin:1rem 0}.chapter-foundation [data-original-document] p,.chapter-foundation [data-document-history] p{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.chapter-foundation button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #065e73;outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:760px){.chapter-actions .studio-button{width:100%}}</style>

<style>.foundation-image{margin:1rem 0 1.4rem}.foundation-image img{display:block;width:100%;height:210px;object-fit:cover;border-radius:3px}.foundation-image figcaption{font-size:.72rem;line-height:1.5;color:#58605d;margin-top:.4rem}.chapter-foundation h2{margin:.7rem 0}.chapter-foundation .chapter-intro{font-size:1.03rem}.chapter-moments{margin-bottom:1rem;font-size:.83rem;gap:.2rem}@media(max-width:760px){.foundation-image img{height:175px}}</style>